   1:Source/html/document.c **** /*
   2:Source/html/document.c ****  * PlutoBrowser — document.c
   3:Source/html/document.c ****  * Complete port of Source/html/document.lua (parse helpers + DOM walk + full
   4:Source/html/document.c ****  * Document.parse pipeline).
   5:Source/html/document.c ****  *
   6:Source/html/document.c ****  * LUA → C FUNCTION MAP (document.lua 1488 lines):
   7:Source/html/document.c ****  *   parseStyle        → doc_parse_style        (last duplicate key wins)
   8:Source/html/document.c ****  *   parseAlign        → doc_parse_align        (lowercased center/right/left only)
   9:Source/html/document.c ****  *   isDisplayNone     → doc_is_display_none    (hidden/popover/display:none)
  10:Source/html/document.c ****  *   isInvertedStyle   → doc_is_inverted_style  (patterns on lowercased value)
  11:Source/html/document.c ****  *   parseBoxSpacing   → doc_parse_box_spacing  (strict num, halved, left-only pad)
  12:Source/html/document.c ****  *   concatNodeText    → doc_concat_node_text
  13:Source/html/document.c ****  *   validHref         → doc_valid_href         ("", "#…", javascript:, data:)
  14:Source/html/document.c ****  *   serializeSvgNode  → doc_serialize_svg_node
  15:Source/html/document.c ****  *   Document.parse    → document_parse (+ document_free)
  16:Source/html/document.c ****  *     Lua closure state (state.*) → Walker struct; Lua recursive walk(node) →
  17:Source/html/document.c ****  *     iterative frame stack (push_enter/push_exit/WFrame) with one recursion
  18:Source/html/document.c ****  *     level for table cells; Lua 1-based table.insert semantics preserved at
  19:Source/html/document.c ****  *     every call site (verified against capture batteries P18/P19).
  20:Source/html/document.c ****  *
  21:Source/html/document.c ****  * Every helper reproduces the Lua reference's observable behavior, including
  22:Source/html/document.c ****  * its quirks (each verified against the verbatim Lua code — see MASTER_TODO):
ARM GAS  /var/folders/65/xyhbx3_n6nd_hs7j3p9nfwv80000gn/T//ccrc7lPq.s 			page 3


  23:Source/html/document.c ****  *   - parseStyle: "([%w%-]+)%s*:%s*([^;]+)" — the LAST duplicate key wins;
  24:Source/html/document.c ****  *     unparseable segments (no valid "key:") do NOT abort the scan, the
  25:Source/html/document.c ****  *     gmatch simply continues with the segment AFTER the next ';'.
  26:Source/html/document.c ****  *   - parseBoxSpacing: num() uses strict tonumber on the component (only the
  27:Source/html/document.c ****  *     '%' stripped) — "10px" is NOT a number and the component is dropped.
  28:Source/html/document.c ****  *     Component values are halved (floor). padding applies only to LEFT.
  29:Source/html/document.c ****  *   - isInvertedStyle patterns run against the LOWERCASED style value (they
  30:Source/html/document.c ****  *     come from parseStyle, which lowercases values).
  31:Source/html/document.c ****  *   - validHref rejects "", "#…", javascript:, data: (case-insensitive).
  32:Source/html/document.c ****  *   - parseAlign returns the LOWERCASED value only for center/right/left.
  33:Source/html/document.c ****  * Attributes arrive as raw (key, value) pairs — exactly like tok.attrs in
  34:Source/html/document.c ****  * Lua — and every helper parses attrs["style"] internally via parseStyle.
  35:Source/html/document.c ****  */
